Package: rfskiosk-pkg
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Ian Bowditch <ibowditch@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @SIZE@
Section: misc
Priority: optional
Depends: pipx, crudini, pcscd, chromium | chromium-browser, polkitd | policykit-1, systemd, udev
Recommends: rfstag-acsvas, wlr-randr
Conflicts: nfcserver3
Replaces: nfcserver3
Description: RFStag sign-in kiosk: system integration
 Browser kiosk service, and plug-and-play support for the NFC readers:
 Sony RC-S380, VTAP100 and ACS ACR1552U. Plugging a reader in starts its
 service (udev), unplugging stops it, and several readers can be attached
 at once.
 .
 The reader programs themselves come from the rfskiosk2 Python package,
 installed with pipx for user pi (~pi/.local/bin). Google Wallet phone taps
 on the ACR1552U also need rfstag-acsvas.
